Template: firewall-agent/manager-url
Type: string
Default:
Description: Firewall manager URL
 The URL of the firewall manager, including scheme and port
 (e.g. https://fwm.example.com:443). The agent uses this to enroll and to
 pull its assigned policy.
 .
 Leave empty to configure it later by editing
 /etc/firewall-agent/config.toml.

Template: firewall-agent/fqdn
Type: string
Default:
Description: Host FQDN
 The fully-qualified domain name of this host. It is used as the
 certificate common name during enrollment.
 .
 Leave empty to use the system's FQDN.

Template: firewall-agent/enroll-token
Type: password
Default:
Description: Enrollment token
 The one-time enrollment token shown in the manager web UI (Hosts >
 Enroll). If provided, enrollment starts immediately after install and
 you only need to approve the host in the manager.
 .
 Leave empty to enroll later with:
   sudo fw-agent enroll --manager-url <URL> --token <TOKEN> --fqdn <FQDN>
